  "concept": {
    "movement": "A low, steady forward crab scuttle with a cautious five-group wave gait. The supplied asymmetric right fore-fork keeps its two pointed blades together, with six actual contacts and a coherent armored carapace. Faster travel lengthens reach and increases cadence.",
    "attack": "The crab braces its pointed legs, draws a claw back, then snaps it forward; a following mirrored claw snap gives a short aggressive double strike. Actual movable fingers close coherently around their measured hinge.",
    "death": "The carapace drops onto a measured balanced underside bearing, the walking limbs relax outward and both claws settle in front. The final pose is held still."
